    "evidence": "Root cause / sink: AbstractUnArchiver.extractFile(File srcF, File dir, InputStream, String entryName, ...) in src/main/java/org/codehaus/plexus/archiver/AbstractUnArchiver.java. Line 309: `final File f = FileUtils.resolveFile( dir, entryName );` resolves an archive-controlled entryName against the extraction directory with no path-traversal / containment check. Trust boundary: entryName originates from an untrusted archive (tar or zip) supplied as AbstractUnArchiver's sourceFile \u2014 attacker-controlled archive content crosses into filesystem write operations. Three concrete sink operations off the same unchecked f/dirF all must be guarded: (1) line 313 overwrite/lastModified check on the unvalidated path; (2) lines 319-322 `final File dirF = f.getParentFile(); if (dirF != null) { dirF.mkdirs(); }` creating arbitrary parent directories outside the destination tree; (3) line ~338 `out = new FileOutputStream( f );` writing attacker-controlled content to the unvalidated resolved path (arbitrary file write / potential RCE via overwriting scripts, cron files, etc.). All three sinks are reached from TWO distinct untrusted sources that funnel entryName into this same sink: TAR (TarUnArchiver.java:113 te.getName() -> AbstractUnArchiver.java:304/309/319/322/338, exercised directly by this PoV) and ZIP (AbstractZipUnArchiver.java lines 93-95 ZipEntryFileInfo.getName() using UnicodePathExtraField or zipEntry.getName() -> line 178 -> lines 218/222 extractFileIfIncluded -> the identical AbstractUnArchiver sink, NOT exercised by this PoV but sharing the identical root cause/vulnerable method). Verified empirically: running the PoV against baseline code writes the marker file to workRoot/pov-escaped-marker.txt (outside dest/) and exits 0. Inserting a containment check immediately after FileUtils.resolveFile(dir, entryName) (rejecting any resolved path not equal to or under dir) causes the PoV to throw ArchiverException and exit 1; this experimental patch was reverted afterward (confirmed via git diff/grep \u2014 no product/test files remain modified).",
