    "notes": "The PoV targets the tar trace (alert groups 1 and 3: TarUnArchiver.java:113 -> AbstractUnArchiver.java:304/309/313 and .../319/322/338) because it is the shortest, most direct source-to-sink path in the alert and requires no plexus-container DI (TarUnArchiver is instantiated directly and driven through its public extract() API with only a ConsoleLogger). Alert group 2's zip traces (AbstractZipUnArchiver.java lines 93-95/178/218/222 -> AbstractUnArchiver.java:304/309/319/322) converge on the exact same AbstractUnArchiver.extractFile() sink and are not separately exercised by this PoV, but are documented in evidence/regression_hint since a fix scoped only to the tar call site would leave the zip path exploitable. Verified live in the project container via the docker wrapper: exit 0 on baseline (vulnerable), exit 1 after an experimental containment-check patch, which was then reverted, leaving the working tree clean except for the new .security-pipeline/pov/ files (PovPathTraversal.java, run_pov.sh).",
    "pov_command": "bash .security-pipeline/pov/run_pov.sh",
    "pov_path": ".security-pipeline/pov/PovPathTraversal.java",
    "regression_hint": "Invariant a correct fix must enforce: for every archive entry (tar and zip alike), the File returned by resolving entryName against the destination directory (currently FileUtils.resolveFile(dir, entryName) at AbstractUnArchiver.java:309) must have a canonical/normalized path equal to dir or strictly nested beneath it (canonicalPath.startsWith(dir.getCanonicalPath() + File.separator)), checked BEFORE any of: the overwrite/lastModified check (~line 313), dirF.mkdirs() (~line 322), SymlinkUtils.createSymbolicLink/f.mkdirs() for directory entries, and new FileOutputStream(f) (~line 338). On violation, extraction of that entry must fail (throw ArchiverException) or be skipped \u2014 not silently written outside destDirectory. Because both TarUnArchiver and AbstractZipUnArchiver funnel into this single extractFile() method, the fix should live in (or be invoked from) AbstractUnArchiver.extractFile() itself so it covers both call sites; a fix applied only at one call site (e.g. only in TarUnArchiver) would leave the zip path exploitable and vice versa. Known bypass variants the fix must also block: plain \"../\" traversal (used here), nested \"../../../\", absolute path entry names (e.g. \"/etc/cron.d/evil\"), Windows-style backslash traversal (\"..\\\\..\\\\evil\"), entries using the Unicode Extra Field path (AbstractZipUnArchiver.java line 94, new String(unicodePath.getUnicodeName(), \"UTF-8\")) which can encode a different traversing name than zipEntry.getName(), and symlink entries (symlinkDestination) that could point outside destDirectory even when the entry name itself is contained (SymlinkUtils.createSymbolicLink(f, new File(symlinkDestination)) \u2014 a related sink not covered by this PoV that a comprehensive fix should also validate).",
